61	WorkPackage	45	4	**Batch determination — municipal witness-test waiver batch (record date 07/14/2025).**\nPrepared for Standards Engineering (Evan Solberg) in support of WP #45 and the 08/15/2025 Alleron Municipal League response.\n\n**1. Batch scope (the record).** The batch is the six municipal commissioning checklists Checklist_Cravenwood_High.pdf through Checklist_Tresbay_Community_Center.pdf (filed 06/15–06/24/2025), reconciled against the DER Program commissioning records (this case, the commissioning-wiki pages for the six checklists, and the Program Office equipment/queue registers as of 07/14/2025).\n\n**2. Arrays still in scope as of 07/14/2025 (5 of 6).** Tresbay Community Center Array (PXA-2025-0061) withdrew its request on 07/09/2025 (per this case's scope note) and is OUT of the batch. The five remaining arrays are in scope — Cravenwood High, Darnwick Elementary, Holcott Library, Lockmere Middle, Marden Falls WRF. None has been issued PTO; all are pre-PTO with witness-test disposition pending.\n\n**3. Certified Equipment List carriage (current CEL = CEL-2025-Q2, published 04/30/2025, Doc no. CEL-2025-Q2).** For each in-scope array the installed inverter/PCE was looked up against the body of CEL-2025-Q2:\n\n- **Cravenwood High School** (PXA-2024-0779; 860 kW; ALN-137) — Solmery Power SM-215K-3P → **CARRIED** (CEL-2025-Q2 Inverters: SM-215K-3P, 215 kW, UL 1741-SB, 11/18/2024, "Carried from CEL-2024-Q4 (Q4 addendum listing)").\n- **Lockmere Middle School** (PXA-2024-0793; 720 kW; ALN-152) — Torvane Electric TE-180K (×4) → **CARRIED** (CEL-2025-Q2 Inverters: TE-180K, 180 kW, UL 1741-SB, 12/09/2024, "Carried from CEL-2024-Q4 (Q4 addendum listing)").\n- **Marden Falls WRF** (980 kW) — Solmery Power SM-245K-3P (×4) → **CARRIED** (CEL-2025-Q2 Inverters: SM-245K-3P, 245 kW, UL 1741-SB, 01/27/2025, "Carried from CEL-2024-Q4 (Q4 addendum listing)").\n- **Darnwick Elementary** (640 kW) — Arvexa PV-750 → **NOT CARRIED**. No "Arvexa" model on CEL-2025-Q2 Inverters or PCS tabs; none on the superseded CEL-2024-Q4 either. ENG-PRC-014 §3/§4.1 → on-site witness test required; the checklist's "waiver eligible" mark was a batch-level copy-forward (Section 6 notes).\n- **Holcott Public Library** (510 kW) — Selvix SV-720 → **NOT CARRIED**. No "Selvix" model on CEL-2025-Q2. The checklist footnote cites only the SUPERSEDED CEL-2024-Q4 (Selvix SV-720, 720 kW, UL 1741-SB, 10/31/2024, "Initial listing this edition"), not carried forward into CEL-2025-Q2. ENG-PRC-014 §3 (corollaries 3, 5) / §4.1 → on-site witness test required.\n\n**4. Witness-test scope (municipal arrays that need an on-site witness test): Darnwick Elementary and Holcott Public Library.** Not waiver-eligible (installed inverter not on the current CEL). Per ENG-PRC-014 §4.2, an on-site witness test is required before PTO. The waiver disposition itself is reserved to Standards Engineering and is not made here.\n\n**5. Waiver-eligible (carried) — disposition reserved to Standards Engineering: Cravenwood High, Lockmere Middle, Marden Falls WRF.** Per ENG-PRC-014 §4.1, eligibility is a necessary but not sufficient condition; the written waiver disposition is for Standards Engineering.\n\n**6. Arrays the SOC can be asked to release as of 07/14/2025: Lockmere Middle and Marden Falls WRF.** The SOC's PTO gate is live telemetry per TCS-02 §5 (SOC PTO-Hold Log DER-EQP-SOC-PTOH, as of 07/14/2025). Lockmere (RTU-LKM-171-04; live telemetry verified with SOC 06/17/2025, TKT-25-04188) and Marden Falls (RTU installed; SCADA verified end-to-end with SOC per TCS-02 §5) already meet the SOC telemetry gate and have carried equipment (waiver path); only the Standards Engineering waiver disposition stands between them and PTO. The other three in-scope arrays (Cravenwood, Darnwick, Holcott) cannot be released by the SOC as of 07/14/2025 — their utility-owned RTU is not yet installed (telemetry pending); Darnwick and Holcott additionally require an on-site witness test. (None of the six municipal batch arrays appears on the SOC PTO-Hold Log, which lists seven other construction-complete sites held on telemetry grounds.)\n\n**7. Scheduling items logged.** One scheduling item per not-carried array, both **Open**, assigned to Evan Solberg, start 07/14/2025, due 08/15/2025:\n- **WP #47** — Holcott Public Library Array witness test (Selvix SV-720 not on CEL-2025-Q2; was on superseded CEL-2024-Q4).\n- **WP #48** — Darnwick Elementary School Array witness test (Arvexa PV-750 not on CEL-2025-Q2).\nEach carries the tests to be performed and their basis, who performs and witnesses, and the prerequisites that must be on file first.\n\n**8. Reconciliation and case closure.** Arrays named in the witness-test package = {Darnwick, Holcott}; scheduling items standing on this case = {WP #47 (Holcott), WP #48 (Darnwick)}. The two agree (2 = 2). Case closed.\n\n**9. Package document.** Municipal_Witness_Test_Package.docx filed in the Program Office municipal commissioning folder (/DER_Program/Commissioning/Municipal/) in the document store, giving each determination with its basis and the carriage call one way or the other.\n\n— DER Program Office (OpenProject Admin), record date 07/14/2025.	2026-11-22 12:52:43.730832+00	2	2026-11-22 12:55:05.616605+00	Journal::WorkPackageJournal	121	{}	["2026-11-22 12:52:43.730832+00",)	f
