109	1	3	Schedule on-site witness test — Holcott Public Library Array (inverter Selvix SV-720 not carried on CEL-2025-Q2; was on superseded CEL-2024-Q4)	**Scheduling item — on-site witness test required before PTO.**\n\n**Array:** Holcott Public Library Array — Town of Holcott (Alleron Municipal League member). Site: 80 Old Mill Road, Holcott, Alleron 84HO. Nameplate 510 kW AC; POI utility secondary, service transformer T-4. DER class: Commercial small-scale (500 kW–1 MW). Checklist CX-HOL-LIB-01, Rev 0, 06/17/2025.\n\n**Installed inverter (as commissioned):** Selvix SV-720 (cover sheet; footnote ¹).\n\n**Why a witness test is required:** The installed inverter is **not carried on the current Certified Equipment List, CEL-2025-Q2** (published 04/30/2025; Doc no. CEL-2025-Q2). No “Selvix” model appears on the CEL-2025-Q2 Inverters or Power Control Systems tabs. The checklist footnote cites only the SUPERSEDED edition — “Selvix SV-720 listed in CEL-2024-Q4 (published 10/31/2024)” — and that listing was not carried forward into CEL-2025-Q2 (confirmed against the superseded workbook: Selvix SV-720, 720 kW, UL 1741-SB, 10/31/2024, “Initial listing this edition”). Under the Witness Test & Waiver Procedure (ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3) §3 (corollaries 3 and 5) and §4.1, a listing that appeared solely on a superseded CEL edition confers no waiver eligibility once the successor edition (CEL-2025-Q2, effective 04/30/2025) takes effect; the facility is ineligible for a waiver and an on-site witness test is required before PTO. The checklist’s “witness test: waiver eligible” mark is overridden by the current-CEL lookup.\n\n**Tests to be performed (basis):** Per ENG-PRC-014 §4.2, testing per IEEE 1547.1, including at minimum: (a) protective-function trip tests (27/59, 81U/81O, 25, 32 as configured) against the approved settings sheet; (b) anti-islanding function test (IEEE 1547.1); (c) voltage and frequency ride-through verifications per DIS-01 Rev 4 §6 (Category II). Basis: ENG-PRC-014 §4.2; IEEE 1547.1; DIS-01 Rev 4 §6; approved protection settings sheet / coordination study on file.\n\n**Who performs / witnesses:** Performed by the customer (Town of Holcott) or its commissioning agent (Alleniom Field Services Crew 12; field engineer M. Halbrook, P.E., AFE-1042) with qualified personnel, calibrated instrumentation, and the approved test plan (ENG-PRC-014 §4.2). Witnessed by an Alleniom Utilities witness engineer — independent of the commissioning agent of record — assigned by Standards Engineering, who records measured values and pass/fail per test point and dispositions the test (ENG-PRC-014 §4.2–§4.3). Scheduled by the DER Program Office commissioning coordinator.\n\n**What must be on file first (prerequisites to PTO):**\n1. Completed commissioning checklist marked “witness test required” with the CEL edition consulted (CEL-2025-Q2) and the finding that Selvix SV-720 is not carried — Sections A–D already Pass on file (06/17/2025).\n2. Approved protection settings sheet / coordination study (checklist Section B).\n3. Customer/commissioning-agent test plan, calibrated-instrumentation list with current calibration certificates, and qualified-personnel designation.\n4. Witness engineer’s signed test record (instrument IDs, measured values, pass/fail per test point, signature, date) — produced at the test.\n5. Live telemetry to the SOC per TCS-02 §5 (utility-owned RTU installed and SCADA verified end-to-end). **NOTE:** Holcott telemetry is PENDING — RTU allocation pending, equipment not allocated (checklist Section E); must close before PTO (SOC will not release without it).\n\nPTO shall not be issued until both the signed witness-test disposition (item 4) and live telemetry (item 5) are on file (ENG-PRC-014 §4.3; TCS-02 §5). On-site witness testing is not to be deferred to a post-PTO date (ENG-PRC-014 §4.2).\n\n**Waiver disposition:** Not applicable — the facility is not waiver-eligible. Reserved to Standards Engineering.\n\n**Case:** DER Program Backlog Review — WP #45 “Process the municipal witness-test waiver batch.” Record date 07/14/2025; League response due 08/15/2025.	2025-08-15	\N	1	11	9	\N	4	\N	\N	2025-07-14	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	\N	t	25	f	\N	\N
