48	1	3	Schedule on-site witness test — Darnwick Elementary School Array (inverter Arvexa PV-750 not carried on CEL-2025-Q2)	**Scheduling item — on-site witness test required before PTO.**\n\n**Array:** Darnwick Elementary School Array — Darnwick Community School District (Alleron Municipal League member). Site: 44 Willowvale Avenue, Darnwick, Alleron 21DA. Nameplate 640 kW; POI secondary service, school-building main switchgear. DER class: Commercial small-scale (500 kW–1 MW). Checklist COMM-CHK-DARN-ELEM, Rev 0, 06/2025.\n\n**Installed inverter (as commissioned):** Arvexa PV-750 (cover sheet; factory profile per Section 2).\n\n**Why a witness test is required:** The installed inverter is **not carried on the current Certified Equipment List, CEL-2025-Q2** (published 04/30/2025; Doc no. CEL-2025-Q2). No “Arvexa” model appears on the CEL-2025-Q2 Inverters tab or the Power Control Systems tab, and none appeared on the superseded CEL-2024-Q4. Under the Witness Test & Waiver Procedure (ENG-PRC-014 Rev 3) §3 and §4.1, an inverter not present in the body of the current CEL edition makes the facility ineligible for a witness-test waiver; an on-site witness test is required before PTO. The checklist’s “witness test: waiver eligible” mark was a batch-level copy-forward (Section 6 notes) and is overridden by the current-CEL lookup.\n\n**Tests to be performed (basis):** Per ENG-PRC-014 §4.2, testing per IEEE 1547.1, including at minimum: (a) protective-function trip tests (27/59, 81U/81O, 25, 32 as configured) against the approved settings sheet; (b) anti-islanding function test (IEEE 1547.1); (c) voltage and frequency ride-through verifications per DIS-01 Rev 4 §6 (Category II). Basis: ENG-PRC-014 §4.2; IEEE 1547.1; DIS-01 Rev 4 §6; approved protection settings sheet / coordination study on file.\n\n**Who performs / witnesses:** Performed by the customer (Darnwick Community School District) or its commissioning agent with qualified personnel, calibrated instrumentation, and the approved test plan (ENG-PRC-014 §4.2). Witnessed by an Alleniom Utilities witness engineer — independent of the commissioning agent of record — assigned by Standards Engineering, who records measured values and pass/fail per test point and dispositions the test (ENG-PRC-014 §4.2–§4.3). Scheduled by the DER Program Office commissioning coordinator.\n\n**What must be on file first (prerequisites to PTO):**\n1. Completed commissioning checklist marked “witness test required” with the CEL edition consulted (CEL-2025-Q2) and the finding that Arvexa PV-750 is not carried — Sections 1–4 already Pass on file (06/15/2025).\n2. Approved protection settings sheet / coordination study (checklist Section 2).\n3. Customer/commissioning-agent test plan, calibrated-instrumentation list with current calibration certificates, and qualified-personnel designation.\n4. Witness engineer’s signed test record (instrument IDs, measured values, pass/fail per test point, signature, date) — produced at the test.\n5. Live telemetry to the SOC per TCS-02 §5 (utility-owned RTU installed and SCADA verified end-to-end). **NOTE:** Darnwick telemetry is PENDING — RTU allocation not yet scheduled (checklist Section 5); must close before PTO (SOC will not release without it).\n\nPTO shall not be issued until both the signed witness-test disposition (item 4) and live telemetry (item 5) are on file (ENG-PRC-014 §4.3; TCS-02 §5). On-site witness testing is not to be deferred to a post-PTO date (ENG-PRC-014 §4.2).\n\n**Waiver disposition:** Not applicable — the facility is not waiver-eligible. Any waiver question is reserved to Standards Engineering.\n\n**Case:** DER Program Backlog Review — WP #45 “Process the municipal witness-test waiver batch.” Record date 07/14/2025; League response due 08/15/2025.	2025-08-15	\N	15	11	9	\N	4	8	\N	\N	2026-11-22 12:47:55.330717+00	2026-11-22 12:55:14.483315+00	2025-07-14	\N	\N	1	\N	\N	\N	t	\N	25	f	\N	\N	\N
